ip between environmental proximity and elevation, providing insight into forest dynamics based on human and natural influences at varying altitudes. It simplifies interpretation while accounting for the dataset's spatial and elevation characteristics.\ndf['Proximity_Mean_Ratio'] = df['Proximity_Factor_Avg'] / (df['Elevation'] + 1e-6)\nend\n\n---\n\n### Dropping redundant columns:\n\n#### Column: Soil_Type36\npython\n# Explanation why the column Soil_Type36 is dropped\n# Soil_Type36 has a near-zero mean (Mean = 0.0001) and very low variance (Std = 0.0103), contributing negligible predictive value for forest cover type.\ndf.drop(columns=['Soil_Type36'], inplace=True)\nend\n\n---\n\n#### Column: Soil_Type8\npython\n# Explanation why the column Soil_Type8 is dropped\n# Soil_Type8 has minimal variance (Mean = 0.0003, Std = 0.0186) and occurs in very few instances across the dataset, making it irrelevant for model predictions.\ndf.drop(columns=['Soil_Type8'], inplace=True)\nend\n\n---\n\n#### Column: Soil_Type28\npython\n# Explanation why the column Soil_Type28 is dropped\n# Soil_Type28 has very low variability (Mean = 0.0016, Std = 0.0399), and its lack of occurrence limits its usefulness in predicting forest cover types, so it is removed for efficiency.\ndf.drop(columns=['Soil_Type28'], inplace=True)\nend\n\n---\n\n### Summary:\n1. Added Features:\n   - Elevation_To_Hydrology_3D_Ratio: Incorporates elevation and proximity to water sources in 3D space for better terrain representation.\n   - Combined_Hillshade_Average: Simplifies sunlight exposure throughout the day to model light patterns impacting forest dynamics.\n   - Proximity_Mean_Ratio: Represents proximity factors relative to elevation, balancing anthropogenic and natural influences across terrain types.\n\n2. Dropped Columns:\n   - Soil_Type36, Soil_Type8, Soil_Type28: Removed due to negligible variance, occurrence, and predictive value—streamlining the dataset for better performance and interpretability."), wit